---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Fact from "../components/Fact.astro";
import { edition } from "../lib/facts";
import { REMOVAL_URL, REPO_URL, SLICE_EDITION } from "../lib/config";
import doc from "../data/facts.json";

const queries = Object.values((doc as unknown as { facts: Record<string, { id: string; query_file: string }> }).facts)
  .map((f) => ({ id: f.id, href: `${REPO_URL}/blob/main/${f.query_file}` }))
  .sort((a, b) => a.id.localeCompare(b.id));
---
<Base title="Methodology" description="How Agent Census finds, collects, parses and counts Claude Code setups, and what it cannot see.">
  <h1>Methodology</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    How the census finds Claude Code setups, what it does with them, and what it cannot see.
  </p>

  <h2>This preview</h2>
  {edition.edition === SLICE_EDITION ? (
    <p>
      This edition is a small vertical slice: <Fact id="harnesses_total" /> harnesses holding <Fact id="artifacts_total" />
      parsed files, found by searching for non-fork repos only. It exists to show the pipeline working end to
      end. The full census enumerates every indexed repo, forks included, and is still being collected.
    </p>
  ) : (
    <p>
      This edition is a random sample of the repos the full census had found by its first search, for
      CLAUDE.md files in non-fork repos: <Fact id="harnesses_total" /> harnesses holding <Fact id="artifacts_total" />
      parsed files. Repos with skills, hooks or MCP files but no CLAUDE.md are missing from it, and forks are
      not included. The full census runs every search and is still being collected.
    </p>
  )}

  <h2>The pipeline</h2>
  <ol class="steps">
    <li><strong>Discover.</strong> GitHub code search for CLAUDE.md, <code>.claude/</code>, <code>.mcp.json</code> and
      plugin manifests. Search caps every query, so the crawler splits each query by file size until every
      slice fits, and records whatever cannot be split further as unreachable.</li>
    <li><strong>Harvest.</strong> For each repo found, fetch the harness files and repo metadata, including the
      commit that every example on this site links to. Secrets are redacted before anything is stored.</li>
    <li><strong>Parse.</strong> One parser per file kind: CLAUDE.md sections and imports, settings permissions and
      hooks, skill, agent and command frontmatter, MCP servers, plugin manifests. Malformed files are kept
      and labelled, never dropped.</li>
    <li><strong>Deduplicate.</strong> Exact matches, then normalized text, then near-duplicates by MinHash, plus a
      name key for skills whose text has drifted. This is where the copy rate comes from.</li>
    <li><strong>Detect techniques.</strong> Deterministic detectors read the parsed files and record evidence for
      each technique they find.</li>
    <li><strong>Describe.</strong> A language model reads one representative of each distinct file and says what
      Claude is being made to do. Any quote it gives must appear verbatim in the file, or the answer is
      rejected.</li>
    <li><strong>Group.</strong> Those descriptions are embedded and clustered into use cases. In this preview the
      clusters were too coarse to publish, so use-case pages are off until the full edition.</li>
    <li><strong>Freeze and count.</strong> The edition is frozen and hashed, and every number on the site is
      computed by a named SQL query over the frozen tables. A check re-runs each query and fails the build on
      any drift.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>Validation</h2>
  <p>
    The full edition is validated by machine agreement and planted canaries, not by human labels: two
    independent model passes with agreement scores, synthetic harnesses with known answers run through the
    whole pipeline, and a model audit of each detector's hits and misses. None of that has run on this
    preview, so technique counts here are raw detector output.
  </p>

  <h2>What the census cannot see</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Code search indexes the default branch of public repos, and not all of them. This is a census of
      indexed public default branches.</li>
    <li>Some file sizes have more matches than search will return, so a share of files cannot be reached.
      The full edition counts and publishes them.</li>
    <li>Some repos are deleted or made private between discovery and harvest. They are recorded as missing.</li>
    <li>Every number is for one frozen point in time. Nothing here is live.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Privacy</h2>
  <p>
    Secrets are redacted before storage. Permission settings are reported only in aggregate, never with a
    repo name. Raw file contents are not redistributed in bulk; examples are short excerpts with a link to the
    exact commit. To have a repo left out of future editions, <a href={REMOVAL_URL}>open a removal request</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Queries behind the numbers</h2>
  <p>Edition {edition.edition}, hash <code class="hash">{edition.edition_hash}</code>.</p>
  <ul class="queries">{queries.map((q) => <li><a href={q.href}><code>{q.id}</code></a></li>)}</ul>
</Base>
<style>
  .steps { padding-left: 1.25rem; max-width: 40rem; }
  .steps li { margin-bottom: 0.75rem; }
  .hash { word-break: break-all; font-size: 0.85rem; }
  .queries { columns: 2; padding-left: 1.25rem; }
  code { font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 0.875em; }
</style>
